// Jest Snapshot v1, https://jestjs.io/docs/snapshot-testing

exports[`CLI help interface for 'config-manager migrate applications' should be expected english 1`] = `
"Usage: frodo config-manager migrate applications [options] [host] [realm] [username] [password]

[Experimental] Move a tree that keeps the objects of an application at the paths
of their own kinds (the layout of config-manager before applications) to one
folder per application. The tenant says which objects an application owns, so
the command reads it. It writes each application as "pull applications" does
(realms/<realm>/applications/<name>/), removes the files of the objects the
application owns from the paths of their own kinds (OAuth2 clients, SAML
providers, connectors and mappings; never scripts or circles of trust), and
writes frodo-config-manager.json at the root of the tree last, only if
everything succeeded. An application that cannot be written keeps its files
where they are, and the command can be run again. Use -d to see what would
happen first. The command does not ask: the tree is a working copy, and the
preview is the safeguard. A tree that already keeps one folder per application
is left alone.

Arguments:
  host                                      AM base URL, e.g.: https://cdk.iam.example.com/am. To use a connection profile, just specify a unique substring or alias.
  realm                                     Realm. Specify realm as '/' for the root realm or 'realm' or '/parent/child' otherwise. (default: "alpha" for Identity Cloud tenants, "/" otherwise.)
  username                                  Username to login with. Must be an admin user with appropriate rights to manage authentication journeys/trees. If given without a password, and it matches the username already stored in the connection profile for the target host, frodo uses that profile's stored password instead of requiring it on the command line.
  password                                  Password.

Options:
  --allow-failures                          Report operations that fail, but still exit with code 0. Without this option the command runs every operation, prints a summary of what failed and exits with code 1.
  -C, --config-folder <config-folder-path>  Path to the folder with the config files of "pull oauth2-agents" and "pull saml" (oauth2-agents.json and saml.json). Their entries that name an object an application owns are reported. The files are never changed.
  -d, --dry-run                             Show the folders that would be written and the files that would be removed, and change nothing.
  -h, --help                                Help
  -hh, --help-more                          Help with all options.
  -hhh, --help-all                          Help with all options, environment variables, and usage examples.
"
`;
